<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK C.BANK SAYS NO REV REPO TENDER ON WEDNESDAY.</title>
<headline>SLOVAK C.BANK SAYS NO REV REPO TENDER ON WEDNESDAY.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) said it would not hold a tender for short-term securities repurchase or reverse repurchase on Wednesday.</p>
<p>According to official NBS figures, the banking sector is in a liquidity surplus, with banks' minimum reserve demands fulfilled at 101.31 percent as of Tuesday, after 100.53 percent the previous day.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-521-8402</p>
